            <title>[LU-21086] sanity-sec test_17: quota usage mismatch after 1 MiB write</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21086</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-sec test_17 failed its quota check in do_fops_quota_test():&lt;br/&gt;
1024 != 22604 + 1M after write, fuzz is 224&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failed subtest: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/b4cfc2e6-733a-46d6-aef6-ec2fc69308eb" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/b4cfc2e6-733a-46d6-aef6-ec2fc69308eb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Test set: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/9c00fee4-6dc0-4f02-97b7-e9ff7083fa0d" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/9c00fee4-6dc0-4f02-97b7-e9ff7083fa0d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Session: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/9690345a-0a12-49a6-a0a6-d81f0b032280" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/9690345a-0a12-49a6-a0a6-d81f0b032280&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Configuration: review-ldiskfs-arm, el8.10-x86_64/rocky9.8-aarch64, ldiskfs servers and client. Revision 53236866c207, change 69318 PS2.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The test samples quota usage, writes a synchronous 1 MiB file, syncs, then checks for a 1024 KiB increase within fs_log_size() tolerance. Here usage decreased from 22604 to 1024 KiB. The root cause is not established.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This failure mode predates change 69318, which changes SSH connection reuse in test-framework.sh and leaves this quota check unchanged. Rainshadow found seven earlier occurrences across three other uploaders (October 2025 through July 2026). In the same review-ldiskfs-arm group, change 67482 PS3 failed on July 24 with: 0 != 0 + 1M after write, fuzz is 224.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/0235c334-2a23-405d-a364-bad38e59448b" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/0235c334-2a23-405d-a364-bad38e59448b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/6b1cefb3-3e40-4035-80bf-6fc3c4336157" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/6b1cefb3-3e40-4035-80bf-6fc3c4336157&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
The suite log of another July 24 run confirms the same check failed in test_17:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/043022ab-2bfd-4a92-9cc4-0128865dff4a" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/043022ab-2bfd-4a92-9cc4-0128865dff4a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Frequency: the current 30-day ARM history has one test_17 failure in 1243 non-skipped runs, this occurrence. The supplied baseline excluding this session has 0 failures in 1240 other-change runs. The longer history establishes that the quota-check error predates the patch; no local reproduction was attempted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14730" title="sanity-sec test_17 timeout" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14730"&gt;LU-14730&lt;/a&gt; is a timeout, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14015" title="sanity-sec test_17: @@@@@@ FAIL: test trusted_noadmin:0:c0:0:000, wanted 0 0, got 1 1" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14015"&gt;LU-14015&lt;/a&gt; is a permissions mismatch, and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-6247" title="osd-zfs: sanity-sec test_16, test_22: 27919 != 26845 + 1M after write" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-6247"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-6247&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; concerns ZFS block-size accounting rather than this ldiskfs usage decrease. Searches for the full test name and after-write quota/fuzz errors found no matching LU. Rainshadow suggests EX-13760 for the same error in test_16, but this run has no EX access and cannot verify or link it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69318-ps2-58e9a74425e7 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69318" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69318&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
